component badsetliteral
export Executable

(* NOT A MISSING INFERENCE PASS. `Set[\T\]` is STAMPED by monomorphization,
   which runs before the checker exists, so an element type discoverable only
   by typing the elements cannot be stamped at all. `SeqIterate` is not a
   precedent for deferring it -- that walks a collection that already exists
   and mints nothing.

   REWRITTEN 2026-08-25, AND THE REWRITE IS THE POINT. This file used to write
   `n = {1, 2, 3}`, which now COMPILES: a set literal whose elements are all
   literals of one kind takes that kind, a SHAPE rule that needs no typing and
   so can run before the stamp. The gate went red on a deliberate change and it
   was right to -- the invariant MOVED rather than died.

   `a` IS A LOCAL, NOT A LITERAL, so its type is discoverable only by typing it
   and the refusal still stands. That is the boundary the syntactic default
   stops at, and it is the same boundary the nine comprehension files sit
   behind. *)
run(): () = do
  a: ZZ32 = 1
  n = {a, a}
  println(1)
end
end
